y being created specifically for the Directory Cards componenet on aws.amazon.com/health/case-studies/. When the GCRP decided to add multilingual content to the CSDIR in 2023, the owners of this page only wanted to display the English content in our Directory. Because the Directory Cards component on their page uses an OR operator to pull in content from two tags, they would be unable to add a prefilter condition to look for only English content. This can only be done if the page is using an AND operator. Thus, this tag will be autoapplied to all content that meets the current prefilter conditions. At that point, the page owners can use the AND operator to display content with this tag and GLOBAL#language#english.\u003c/p\u003e\n","dateCreated":"2023-04-26T20:23:44+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-04-26T20:23:44+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#healthfirst20200629sdlkdfhj","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"healthfirst20200629sdlkdfhj","dateCreated":"2022-05-23T21:41:50+0000","dateUpdated":"2023-07-14T23:32:28+0000","additionalFields":{"descriptionSummary":"Wrangling data from increasingly more sources can become unwieldy. In this episode of \u0027This is my Architecture\u0027, we revisit Healthfirst\u0027s Secure Analytics Platform (https://youtu.be/ZqFWOQyQaNQ) to see how they have extended their solution with AWS CloudFormation, Amazon SQS, AWS Step Functions and AWS Lambda to improve coordination of data pipelines. We also learn how they leverage Amazon SageMaker to introduce Machine Learning to their data, to better identify risks factors in determinance of health outcomes.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/healthfirst-logo%401x.327da8037f4b8a0110149a4ce0bdd5ae95bc1479.png","displayLocation":"United States","footerInfoText":"Published Date","industry":"Healthcare","sortDate":"2020-06-29","headlineUrl":"https://youtu.be/XpFNznmRoQ0?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","enableShare"